  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bauxite is an oxide ore of Al. Its formula is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>Formula of malachite is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Formula of calamine is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Formula of calamine is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"
